# Declared absences — paths a live document names in order to say they do not exist.
#
# Format:  <document> :: <token> :: <reason>
#
# Reporting an absence is required conduct here ("a negative finding is a result"), so a
# document that names a missing file on purpose must not be forced to invent one. Every
# entry below is a claim that the named path is DELIBERATELY absent, and the reason says
# why. `tools/resolve_named_paths.py` reports any entry that is no longer named by its
# document, so this file cannot silently rot.
#
# This file is NOT for stale references. If a path is absent because a document was never
# updated, fix the document.

# --- Genres the document law defines and this repository has not built (§7) ---
canon/THE_DOCUMENT_LAW.md :: HOLONIC_OWNERSHIP.md :: the ownership ledger is specified in §1.9 and explicitly "not yet built"
canon/THE_DOCUMENT_LAW.md :: RESULTS.md :: the observation-result genre filename; §1.8 states the live genre is empty
canon/THE_DOCUMENT_LAW.md :: evidence/observations/ :: named as the archived location; the live genre is empty by §1.8

# `.agents/COMMUNE/` needs no entry: it resolves in the frozen laboratory at a07ff376, and
# `/tmp/codex-clipboard-T9jMYB.png` needs none either — an absolute path outside this repository
# is not a claim about this tree.

# --- Named permanent losses. These resolve at no commit in either repository. ---
canon/THE_RECOVERED_LAW.md :: src/soma/runs/ :: the untracked laboratory directory that took the tiger figures and the semantics theorem with it; the citation is the point

