# --- A source constant quoted verbatim, not an existence claim ---
# Surfaced 2026-08-07 when the checker learned to see a directory written without its trailing
# slash. The prose says "whose `DEFAULT_OUTPUT` is *literally*" and then quotes the string; the
# constant really is that, at crates/holonic-engine/examples/curved_receiver_phase_atlas.rs:22.
# It names an output location under `target/`, which is a build directory this checker prunes and
# git ignores, so the token can never resolve and must never be "fixed" by inventing a path.
canon/THE_QUOTE_NETWORK.md :: target/holonic-engine/curved-receiver-phase-atlas-tiger :: verbatim gitignored DEFAULT_OUTPUT constant quoted as historical runtime provenance

# --- Build directories quoted as ignore patterns, not as paths to follow ---
# `.lake/` is Lake's generated-artifact directory. All four mentions quote it as a `.gitignore`
# pattern or a directory KIND ("generated `.lake/` build output is ignored"), never as a path a
# reader should open. It cannot resolve here even where it physically exists, because its only
# contents are `build/` and `packages/` — both in this checker's own PRUNED set.
canon/THE_QUOTE_NETWORK.md :: target/debug/deps :: gitignored Cargo test-binary directory quoted as measured runtime provenance

